    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nProbably a documentation typo, cause `actual behaviour` feels more correct/regex'ish.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.4\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. cd to directory with `*.lua` files\r\n2. `:Pick files`\r\n3. Type `$.lua` -> no results\r\n4. Type `.lua$` -> many results\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nFrom `mini.pick` documentation: `If query starts with $, the match is exact at end`.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nActual behaviour `If query ends with $, the match is exact at end`.\r\n",
